# Every tracked file here is LF today, and this is developed on Windows, where
# a contributor's autocrlf setting otherwise decides what lands in a commit.
# Pinning it is what stops a one-line edit arriving as a whole-file diff.
#
# LF in the working tree as well as in the index: MSVC, clang-cl, CMake and
# every editor in use read LF perfectly well, and a mixed checkout is how the
# phantom diffs start.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.lib binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary

# vcpkg port patches are applied byte for byte against upstream sources, some of
# which are CRLF (CPython's PCbuild). Normalising them would stop them applying.
cmake/vcpkg-ports/**/*.patch -text
